A||||9||Uaana||Body Panel Swap||||1||
Z||000000||Uaana||04-26-2001||10:01 PM||||Looks like I'm going to be the new owner of Tina's rainbow Fiero.. Well The front end is toast and some other panels are shot as well.<BR>Question is:<BR>Is it possible for one guy with nothing but hand tools to remove and replace the existing panels with those from a donor car.<BR>I have an all White 85 SE with a bad motor that is desperate for a use.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tina||04-26-2001||10:37 PM||||For the front end the hand tools will do.<BR>Doorpanel wise you might run into a couple of rivets.(You could drill those out)<BR>The one thing you are going to need is a <BR>rivet-gun for large rivets to put the panels back up. Plus a handful of molding fastners to replace the ones you broke,taking them off.<P>Have fun with it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Tina||||reg||1
Z||000002||Uaana||04-26-2001||11:36 PM||||Thanks Tina, <BR>The front will probably get done on Sunday<BR>I hate bug eyes. That and the rear lenses<BR>The thing I'm worried about is the overhead that stretches back to the fenders.<BR>That and I think I'm gonna just swap the doors. (my glass isn't as scratched up)<P>BTW does that thing really have a Hypertech chip in it?<p>[This message has been edited by Uaana (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tina||04-26-2001||11:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Uaana:<BR><B>The thing I'm worried about is the overhead that stretches back to the fenders.<BR>(edited 04-26-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>What #pic,a bit confused.<BR>Hyperchip? Don't know.<BR>Ask Eric tommorow,if it does he would know.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Uaana||04-27-2001||12:24 AM||||Best pic for the part I'm talking about would be #12 that part connects both sides by wraping up and over the roof.<BR>By the time I've finished it will look pretty much like an 85 SE but I'll keep the rear bumperand lower rear quarters stock.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tina||04-27-2001||01:00 AM||||Slight lapse in memory.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">(Had to go out to garage and check on 84)<BR>Verdict<BR>Easy as well,all one piece.3 or 4 bolts underneath headliner a couple along side<BR>trunk area.(underneath vents)<BR>Watch out for those triangular black pieces on the inside (right next to rear window).<BR>.||||reg||1
Z||000006||84Bill||04-27-2001||10:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B>Slight lapse in memory.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">(Had to go out to garage and check on 84)<BR>Verdict<BR>Easy as well,all one piece.3 or 4 bolts underneath headliner a couple along side<BR>trunk area.(underneath vents)<BR>Watch out for those triangular black pieces on the inside (right next to rear window).<BR>.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Dont forget about the 3 bolts arround the fuel filler neck under the fuel door assembly.<P>||||reg||11
Z||000007||Uaana||04-28-2001||07:29 PM||||Well for a quick update. The coupe nose is mostly on (there was more damage underneath than I expected) And if you ever see the original owner again. Smack him one.. looked like frankenstein was working in the wheel wells and front end.) The signal mounts are so torn up I may end up putting driving lights in there and crossing my fingers.<BR>Car also has 4 new tires and rims. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||04-28-2001||07:51 PM||||read the door article in my cave. You Do Not need to buy a rivet tool and pop rivets for the door skins. <P>The screw rivets listed in that article will work as well or better than OE. A plus is that those rivets are reusable so you can take the skin off again if need be and reuse the rivets.<P>As long as you are carefull, you can break the door skin rivets. They aren't very tough. They just keep the skin from getting caught on something and breaking. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tina||04-28-2001||11:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Uaana:<BR><B> And if you ever see the original owner again. Smack him one.. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL Go for it man.<BR>Forgot to give you picture I found in car.<BR>(Previous owner in Fiero)<BR>Might come in handy for just this purpose. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyways, sounds like the "Rainbow marvel"<BR>found a good home. <P>Good Luck<BR>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
